test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T09:46:53.7691484Z             "body": "Hardens the original MCP entrypoint and independent declarative workflow companion while preserving upstream tool contracts and defaults. Adds bounded cleanup/cancellation, stricter workflow policy, fork-safe production packaging, durable local job internals and reproducible native evidence. The draft remains incomplete and must not be merged or published as release-ready.\n\nLatest source e95f029 fixes fresh live-anchor audit initialization and requires strict TypeScript checks for all test files, runner config and public declarations. Actual validated root births now precede historical traversal; unknown roots and full legacy observations stay conservative. No process-name/age filtering or new PID termination authority. Type dependencies are development-only; assertions, deadlines and runtime defaults remain intact.\n\nLocal verification: Node20/22/24 typecheck passes with library declaration checking; graph/cleanup18 tests on20 and combined26 on22/24; Chromium/Firefox32 cases; fresh176-file production package; real private/inherited20 fresh runs/460 actions; forced-close negative exits1 as expected. Evidence and source hashes are committed. Follow-up audit: npm vulnerabilities0;173 relative Markdown targets exist; limited credential scan retains the unchanged baseline HTTPS fixture key.\n\nLatest completed native82 at bbf4764:1,929 reported test passes/11 failures plus4 failed Windows JSON controls. All original platforms156 each, Docker2, Macmodal3, bounded stderr probes12 and three actual Codex1k clients pass. Windows browser input/cleanup/privacy/origin/retry failures and Mac screenshot/raw1k/synchronous1k deadlines remain unresolved. Historical ownership observations remain unclassified. Healthy later controls do not establish a causal fix.\n\nNative83 is running at e95f029:\n- https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39753138604\n- https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39753138605\n\nRelease blockers, complete evidence and G00–G18 statuses are in docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md and docs/RELEASE_BLOCKERS.md. No merge/publication or access workaround performed.\n",
